.TH "PB-TEAM-SCIM-MAP" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-scim-map - Map a directory group to a team role


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team scim map <team> <group> <admin|billing|auditor|member|none> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Map a directory group, by name or ID, to a team role: admin, billing, auditor or member, or none to remove the mapping. Someone in several mapped groups gets the highest role. With --mapped-only, only members of mapped groups are provisioned and everyone else is removed. Members managed by the directory change only through it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for map

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--mapped-only\fP[=false]
	provision only members of mapped groups


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-scim(1)\fP
